Thanks, that looks like a more fleshed-out idea of what I had in mind. A
separate dispatcher for each type (dipping, applying, etc.) of object
interaction would work nicely, I think.

And if the game uses the Command pattern, the interactions could place a
command object on a queue... done properly, it should allow for commands to
be undone in explore / wizard mode. Not sure how that would work with
varying player speeds (slow, normal, fast, very fast), and multi-turn
actions, though. Perhaps give the command object (or a subclass
representing player commands) a duration, and if it's too high, move it to
a "pending actions" queue. Speed could be represented by the number of
durations that pass before the turn is incremented.

This is actually starting to sound achievable...

